# Release version in docs

Whenever a Shopped app version is released or bumped, supporting download docs must show that same version. Do not leave stale version numbers in user-facing download text.

## Required surfaces

These must match the released `major.minor.patch` from `pubspec.yaml` / the GitHub Release:

- `README.md` Download section (`Current version`, package names, download URLs)
- `docs/index.html` product page (`Get Shopped`, `Current version`, download cards)

Do not rewrite the README versioning *examples* in prose (the ``1.0.0`` → ``1.0.1`` band explanation).

## How to update

Use the repo helper; do not hand-edit version strings when the helper can do it:

```sh
python tool/sync_release_docs.py --version X.Y.Z
```

Or with no argument, to match `pubspec.yaml`:

```sh
python tool/sync_release_docs.py
```

The Release workflow runs this automatically after a successful publish (`Record version in pubspec and docs`). If you change download docs outside that path, still run the helper so versions stay aligned.

## Scope

If you add another download page or install doc that hardcodes the release version, register it in `tool/sync_release_docs.py` (`DOC_PATHS`) and cover it with tests.
